<div  class="usa-modal l-constrain" id="modal-link-check-status-pet-health-certificate" aria-labelledby="modal-link-check-status-pet-health-certificate-heading">
    <button type="button" class="usa-modal__close" aria-label="Close this window" data-close-modal=""></button>
    <div class="usa-modal__content">
        <div class="usa-modal__main">
                                        <h2 class="usa-modal__heading" id="modal-link-check-status-pet-health-certificate-heading">
                    Important Notice for Pet Owners
                </h2>
                                                    


<div  class="c-field">
  <div class="c-field__content">
                      

  <div class="l-constrain c-paragraph c-paragraph--type-wysiwyg c-paragraph--view-mode-default">
        




<div  class="c-field c-field--name-field-wysiwyg c-field--type-text-long c-field--label-hidden">
  <div class="c-field__content"><p>Health certificate endorsements may take several business days and are often completed just 1–2 days before travel. Mailing can add extra time, and incomplete paperwork may delay or prevent endorsement.</p><p><strong>For updates, contact your </strong><a href="https://vsapps.aphis.usda.gov/vsps/public/VetSearch.do?method=display&amp;_gl=1*ed6tbi*_ga*MjEwNTMxNzU3Mi4xNjg0MTU1Nzg0*_ga_NRK0CEY9GC*MTY5MzU4Mjg4Ny4zMDkuMS4xNjkzNTg1MTU1LjAuMC4w"><strong>accredited veterinarian</strong></a><strong>.</strong> They submit your documents and can track endorsement status through the Veterinary Export Health Certification System (VEHCS). Due to high volume, USDA <strong>cannot&nbsp;</strong>provide individual status updates.</p><p><strong>Plan ahead:</strong> Have a backup plan in case your certificate isn’t ready—such as leaving your pet with a caretaker or adjusting travel dates.</p><p><strong>Other tips:</strong></p><ul type="disc"><li>If mailed documents are missing, contact the courier. Lost packages must be reissued through VEHCS by your veterinarian.</li><li>Pet owners cannot submit documents to USDA offices. All submissions must be made by the veterinarian through VEHCS.</li></ul></div></div>

  </div>
      </div></div>

                            </div>
</div>
</div>
</div></div>

</div>
